# The pack's Gradle build. What ships is the archive it produces -- lib/newproject.apk, built before
# packing -- not the toolchain that builds it, the jars it compiles against, or Gradle's state.
#
# The Gradle root is the repository root, so this is a list rather than one directory: `native/`
# holds only the module directory, and everything that builds it sits beside it.
#
# Leading `/` anchors an entry to the package root. It matters here: an unanchored `gradle` matches
# by base name at any depth and would take a `languages/gradle/` with it, shipping a language pack
# short of a language and saying nothing about it.
native
build-libs
/gradle
/build
/.gradle
/.kotlin
gradlew
gradlew.bat
gradle.properties
settings.gradle.kts
build.gradle.kts
package.json
package-lock.json
build.mjs
